---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../consts';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy"
      description="How App-Tipps.com collects, uses and protects personal data, your rights under UK GDPR and EU GDPR, and how to exercise them.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 24 August 2026. This policy replaces all earlier versions.</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        App-Tipps.com is operated by {PUBLISHER.legalName} ("we", "us"), a company registered in England
        and Wales under number {PUBLISHER.companyNumber}, with its registered office at {PUBLISHER.address.street},
        {' '}{PUBLISHER.address.city} {PUBLISHER.address.postcode}, {PUBLISHER.address.country}. We are the data
        controller for personal data collected through this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        For any privacy question or request, contact <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <h3>Information you give us</h3>
      <p>
        If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you put in the message. We use it
        only to handle your enquiry. Legal basis: legitimate interests (responding to correspondence).
        We keep enquiry email for 24 months.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we offer a newsletter subscription and you choose to subscribe, we process the information
        requested by the subscription form for that purpose. You can withdraw consent using the
        unsubscribe method provided with the newsletter or by emailing us.
      </p>
      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <p>
        Our hosting and security infrastructure processes IP addresses and basic request data to deliver
        pages and protect the site from abuse. This is necessary to operate the service securely. We do
        not use these request logs to identify ordinary readers.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not require reader accounts, we do not host comments, and we do not ask readers for payment
        details on App-Tipps.com.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising, analytics and consent</h2>
      <p>
        App-Tipps uses Google Analytics 4 for audience measurement and may serve advertising through
        Google Ad Manager or Google AdSense. These services may process device, browser, approximate
        location and interaction data to measure site and advertising performance. Where consent is
        required, optional storage and personalised advertising remain disabled until that choice has
        been collected.
      </p>
      <p>
        If Google AdSense or Google Ad Manager advertising is enabled for visitors in the European
        Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, App-Tipps will use a Google-certified consent
        management platform integrated with the IAB Europe Transparency and Consent Framework where
        Google requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Depending on services enabled in the future and the choices you make, providers may process data
        needed to deliver advertising, measure performance, limit repeated ads or provide analytics.
        Personalised advertising will only be used where the required consent has been obtained.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> explains the categories of cookies and similar
        technologies that may be used. Once optional services are enabled, the site will also provide the
        controls required to review or change consent choices.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some articles and advertisements may contain affiliate links. If you follow one, an affiliate
        tracking provider and the destination merchant or service may process the click and subsequent
        signup so it can be attributed to App-Tipps. Their processing is subject to their respective
        privacy information. Affiliate content and advertisements are labelled on App-Tipps.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. Data may be processed by service providers that help us host,
        secure and operate the site, and by optional advertising, analytics, consent or newsletter
        providers when those services are enabled. We may also disclose information where required by law
        or where necessary to establish or defend legal claims.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some service providers may process data outside the UK or EEA. Where applicable, transfers are
        handled using the safeguards required for the relevant processing, such as an adequacy decision or
        approved contractual safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live and the processing involved, your data-protection rights may include the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>ask for data to be deleted where the law provides that right;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to certain processing;</li>
        <li>receive eligible data in a portable format;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a> with "Data request"
        in the subject line. If you are unhappy with how a UK data-protection matter is handled, you may
        also contact the UK Information Commissioner's Office.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is written for a general audience and is not intended as a service for children. We do
        not knowingly ask children to create accounts or submit personal information through the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We update this policy when our practices change. The date at the top shows the current version.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
